Article 8 Under any of the following circumstances, no person may act as a private fund manager, or become a controlling shareholder, actual controller, or general partner of a private fund manager:
(1) The circumstances specified in Article 9 of these Regulations;
(2) A private fund manager whose registration has been canceled due to the circumstances specified in Item (3) of the first paragraph of Article 14 of these Regulations, and less than three years have elapsed since the date of cancellation of registration, or being a controlling shareholder, actual controller, or general partner of such a private fund manager;
(3) The business engaged in has a conflict of interest with private fund management;
(4) Having a serious adverse credit record that has not yet been remedied.

Article 9 Under any of the following circumstances, no person may act as a director, supervisor, senior officer, managing partner, or appointed representative of a private fund manager:
(1) Having been sentenced to a criminal penalty for committing crimes of embezzlement, bribery, malfeasance, property infringement, or undermining the order of the socialist market economy;
(2) Having been subjected to an administrative penalty by a financial regulatory authority for a major illegal or irregular act within the last three years;
(3) Having been a director, supervisor, factory director, senior officer, managing partner, or appointed representative who bears personal responsibility for a company or enterprise that has gone into bankruptcy liquidation due to poor management or has had its business license revoked due to illegal acts, and less than five years have elapsed since the date of conclusion of the bankruptcy liquidation or the date of revocation of the business license;
(4) Having a relatively large amount of debt that is due and has not been repaid, or being included in the list of dishonest persons subject to enforcement;
(5) Having been dismissed from a fund manager, fund custodian, securities and futures exchange, securities company, securities depository and clearing institution, futures company, or other institution, or having been a functionary of a state organ, due to illegal acts;
(6) Being a lawyer, certified public accountant, or practitioner of an asset appraisal institution, verification institution, or investment consulting institution whose practice certificate has been revoked or whose qualification has been canceled due to illegal acts, and less than five years have elapsed since the date of revocation or cancellation;
(7) Having served as the legal representative, managing partner, or appointed representative, or as a senior officer bearing responsibility, of a private fund manager whose registration has been canceled due to the circumstances specified in Item (3) of the first paragraph of Article 14 of these Regulations, and less than three years have elapsed since the date of cancellation of registration of such private fund manager.

Article 10 A private fund manager shall, according to law, submit the following materials to the institution entrusted by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council (hereinafter referred to as the registration and recordation institution) and fulfill the registration formalities:
(1) The unified social credit code;
(2) The company's articles of association or the partnership agreement;
(3) Basic information of the shareholders, actual controller, directors, supervisors, senior officers, general partner, managing partner or appointed representative, and information on the beneficial owners of the shareholders, actual controller, and partners;
(4) A letter of commitment ensuring the truthfulness, accuracy, and completeness of the submitted materials and compliance with supervision and administration regulations;
(5) Other materials as prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.
Where a major matter such as the controlling shareholder, actual controller, general partner, managing partner, or appointed representative of a private fund manager changes, it shall fulfill the modification registration formalities with the registration and recordation institution in accordance with the provisions.
The registration and recordation institution shall publish relevant information on private fund managers that have undergone registration.
No unit or individual may, without registration, use the words "fund" or "fund management" or similar names for investment activities, unless otherwise provided by laws, administrative regulations, and the State.

Article 11 A private fund manager shall perform the following duties:
(1) Raise funds according to law and handle the recordation of the private fund;
(2) Manage the property of different private funds under its management separately, maintain separate accounts, and conduct investments;
(3) Manage the private fund and conduct investments in accordance with the provisions of the fund contract, and establish an effective risk control system;
(4) Determine the profit distribution plan of the private fund in accordance with the provisions of the fund contract and distribute profits to investors;
(5) Provide investors with information related to the private fund management business activities in accordance with the provisions of the fund contract;
(6) Preserve records, account books, statements, and other relevant materials of the private fund property management business activities;
(7) Other duties as prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council and as agreed in the fund contract.
Where an investment fund is established by raising funds through non-public offerings, the private fund manager shall also, in its own name, exercise litigation rights or perform other legal acts for the benefit of the private fund property.

Article 12 The shareholders, actual controller, and partners of a private fund manager shall not engage in the following acts:
(1) Making false capital contributions, withdrawing capital contributions, entrusting others to make capital contributions, or accepting entrustment from others to make capital contributions;
(2) Interfering with the business activities of the private fund manager without due process such as a resolution of the shareholders' meeting or the board of directors;
(3) Requiring the private fund manager to use private fund property for the benefit of itself or others, thereby harming the interests of investors;
(4) Other acts prohibited by laws, administrative regulations, and the provisions of the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 13 A private fund manager shall continuously meet the following requirements:
(1) Having a sound financial condition and having operating funds commensurate with the type of business and the scale of assets under management;
(2) The legal representative, managing partner or appointed representative, and the senior officer responsible for investment management shall hold a certain percentage of equity or property interests in the private fund manager in accordance with the provisions of the securities regulatory authority under the State Council, unless otherwise provided by the State;
(3) Other requirements as prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.

Article 14 Where a private fund manager falls under any of the following circumstances, the registration and recordation institution shall promptly cancel the registration of the private fund manager and make a public announcement:
(1) Applying for cancellation of registration voluntarily;
(2) Dissolving according to law, being revoked according to law, or being declared bankrupt according to law;
(3) Being subject to legal liability for major illegal acts such as illegal fundraising or illegal business operations;
(4) Failing to record the first private fund within 12 months from the date of registration;
(5) After all the private funds under its management have been liquidated, failing to record a new private fund within 12 months from the date of completion of the liquidation;
(6) Other circumstances as prescribed by the securities regulatory authority under the State Council.
Before canceling the registration of a private fund manager, the registration and recordation institution shall notify the private fund manager to liquidate the private fund property or transfer the responsibilities of private fund management to another registered private fund manager according to law.

Article 22: A private fund manager shall, within 20 working days from the date of completion of the offering of the private fund, submit the following materials to the registration and filing institution for recordation:
(1) the fund contract;
(2) the custody agreement or the institutional measures for ensuring the safety of private fund property;
(3) the documentation evidencing the private fund property;
(4) the basic information of the investors, the subscription amount, the number of fund shares held, and the information related to their beneficial owners;
(5) other materials as prescribed by the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.
A private fund shall have a paid-in offering fund size that ensures basic investment capacity and risk resistance. The registration and filing institution shall implement classified public disclosure based on the fund's offering size and other circumstances, and where the total amount of funds offered or the number of investors reaches the prescribed standards, it shall report to the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.

Article 30: A private fund manager, a private fund custodian, and their practitioners shall not engage in the following acts:
(1) commingling their own property or the property of others with private fund property;
(2) using private fund property or taking advantage of their positions to seek benefits for persons other than the investors;
(3) misappropriating or embezzling private fund property;
(4) disclosing non-public information obtained by virtue of their positions, and using such information to engage in or explicitly or implicitly induce others to engage in related securities or futures trading activities;
(5) other acts prohibited by laws, administrative regulations, and the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.

Article 32: The information provided and submitted by a private fund manager, a private fund custodian, and their practitioners shall be true, accurate, and complete, and they shall not engage in the following acts:
(1) false records, misleading statements, or material omissions;
(2) making predictions on investment performance;
(3) promising investors that the principal will not be lost or promising minimum returns;
(4) other acts prohibited by laws, administrative regulations, and the securities regulatory authority of the State Council.

Article 35: For the purposes of these Regulations, "venture capital fund" means a private fund that meets the following conditions:
(1) the investment scope is limited to unlisted enterprises, except for the unsold portion of the shares held by the fund after the invested enterprise goes public and their placement portion;
(2) the fund name includes the words "venture capital fund", or the business scope of the company or partnership includes the words "engaging in venture capital activities";
(3) the fund contract reflects the venture capital strategy;
(4) it does not use leveraged financing, except as otherwise provided by the state;
(5) the minimum duration of the fund complies with the relevant provisions of the state;
(6) other conditions prescribed by the state.

Article 37: The securities regulatory authority of the State Council shall implement differentiated supervision and management for venture capital funds that distinguishes them from other private funds:
(1) optimizing the business environment for venture capital funds and simplifying the registration and filing procedures;
(2) implementing differentiated supervision and management for venture capital funds that conduct lawful fund raising, compliant investment, and honest operation in terms of fund offering, investment operation, risk monitoring, on-site inspection, etc., and reducing the frequency of inspections;
(3) providing facilitation for venture capital funds that primarily engage in long-term investment, value investment, and transformation of major scientific and technological achievements in terms of investment exit and other aspects.

Article 39: The securities regulatory authority of the State Council shall exercise supervision and management over private fund business activities, and perform the following duties according to law:
(1) formulating regulations and rules on the supervision and management of private fund business activities;
(2) exercising supervision and management over private fund managers, private fund custodians, and other institutions engaging in private fund business activities, and investigating and punishing illegal acts;
(3) guiding, inspecting, and supervising registration, filing, and self-discipline management activities;
(4) other duties prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 40: When performing its duties according to law, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council has the power to take the following measures:
(1) conducting on-site inspections of private fund managers, private fund custodians, and private fund service institutions, and requiring them to submit relevant business materials;
(2) entering the premises where suspected illegal acts occur to investigate and collect evidence;
(3) interrogating the parties and the entities and individuals related to the matter under investigation, and requiring them to provide explanations on matters related to the matter under investigation;
(4) inspecting and copying materials such as property rights registrations and communication records related to the matter under investigation;
(5) inspecting and copying securities trading records, registration and transfer records, financial accounting materials, and other relevant documents and materials of the parties and the entities and individuals related to the matter under investigation; and sealing up documents and materials that may be transferred, concealed, or destroyed;
(6) inquiring, according to law, into account information of the parties and those related to the matter under investigation;
(7) other measures prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
For the purpose of preventing private fund risks and maintaining market order, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council may take measures such as ordering rectification, regulatory interviews, and issuing warning letters.

Article 42 Where the securities regulatory authority of the State Council discovers that a private fund manager violates laws or regulations, or that its internal governance structure and risk control management do not comply with the provisions, it shall order rectification within a specified time limit; if the rectification is not made within the time limit, or the act seriously endangers the stable operation of the private fund manager and impairs the legitimate rights and interests of investors, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council may, as the case may be, take the following measures against it:
(1) Ordering suspension of part or all of its business;
(2) Ordering replacement of its directors, supervisors, senior officers, managing partners or designated representatives, or restricting their rights;
(3) Ordering the shareholders or partners who are responsible for the violation to transfer their equity or partnership shares, restricting the exercise of rights by such shareholders or partners;
(4) Ordering the private fund manager to engage or designate a third-party institution to conduct an audit of the private fund's property, with the relevant costs to be borne by the private fund manager.
Where a private fund manager engages in illegal business or experiences a major risk that seriously endangers market order or impairs investors' interests, the securities regulatory authority of the State Council may, in addition to the measures provided in the preceding paragraph, also take measures against the private fund manager such as designating another institution to take over, or notifying the registration and filing institution to cancel the registration.
